# Keep package-lock.json portable across registries.
#
# The lockfile pins canonical public-registry (registry.npmjs.org) tarball
# URLs. Each environment fetches them through its own configured registry:
#   - CI (GitHub-hosted runners) reaches registry.npmjs.org directly.
#   - Developers behind the internal npm proxy have the host rewritten to the
#     proxy at fetch time by the setting below (their own .npmrc sets the
#     proxy as the active registry).
#
# Never commit an internal proxy host into the lockfile. If `npm install`
# introduces one (it can, when run behind the proxy), run `npm run lockfile:fix`
# before committing — CI enforces this via `npm run lockfile:check`.
replace-registry-host=npmjs
